       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Higher doses haven't been shown to work better, and they raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and seizures. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function) would justify going above the maximum.\n\nIs it possible you meant one of these?\n- **200 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **A lower dose.** For depression or anxiety, the usual start is 25\u201350 mg daily, titrated up.\n- **A different drug or dose**, if 400 mg was a slip.\n\nIf you do want 400 mg for a specific reason, tell me the indication and that you want it entered as written. I can add a note to the order, and pharmacy will probably want to verify it. Otherwise, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
